$\mu\leftarrow(1-\lambda)\mu_{\mathrm{FR}}+\lambda\mu_{\mathrm{EN}}$. This variant retains both contexts and Eq.~(2), then uses a single conditional DiT branch plus the unconditional branch (Secs.~5.3, 6.1). Velocity mixing is used for all held-out test and transfer runs.

We refer to each compared configuration as an arm. A: real $r_{\mathrm{FR}}$. B: synthetic $r_{\mathrm{EN}}$. C: proposed guidance at $\lambda^{\!*}=0.33$. Cascade: unconditioned English from VoxCPM2, then Seed-VC transfers $r_{\mathrm{FR}}$ timbre on every utterance.

Held-out test (B1-CNS-test): 20 MLS French speakers $\times$ 20 English texts $\times$ 3 seeds, item-matched $n=1200$/arm including the cascade; speakers are disjoint.

